  "notes": "Large guest roster split across a 'GUESTS' section (#1-122) and a 'PANELISTS' section (#123-150) on one Guests page; both sections picked, two guests under 'CANCELED' (Amelia Tyler, Persephone Valentine) skipped. A few org/collective entries with no single named person (Games Done Quick, Jackbox Games, National Association of Voice Actors, Stream For A Cause, PAX Pokemon League) are kept as single guest entries because the site itself gives each its own guest card/bio page like any individual. Pierce Courchaine and Tyler Jacobson have no known-for text on their cards at all (only venue/day), so known-for is left blank for both rather than guessed. JSON-LD gave slightly different UTC timestamps (Apr 21 22:00 - Apr 25 06:00); used the page's own visible 'Show Dates & Hours' (Thu Apr 22 - Sun Apr 25) instead. Cover: picked the 2026/backgrounds 'enforcer' split-background key art over a crowd photo from a past Omegathon and a plain gradient; no og/twitter image, just the dateless logo. 2026-10-05 re-verify: current -- fresh extraction of the guests page itself (not just the homepage) leads with 'Apr 22 - 25, 2027 Thomas M. Menino Convention & Exhibition Center' and every card carries this edition's day-specific schedule tags (Panels/Autographing Thu-Sun); the same CANCELED section with only Amelia Tyler and Persephone Valentine still appears and all 150 picks still match exactly, so the lineup is unchanged. REFUTE-pass (2026-10-05): upheld, all 150 proven -- a further independent --fresh re-extraction again leads with 'Apr 22 - 25, 2027 Thomas M. Menino Convention & Exhibition Center' and confirms every guest card still carries a specific Thu/Fri/Sat/Sun-style schedule tag matching this edition's own Thu-Sun calendar (e.g. #150 Vince Perrino still 'Panels Thu'); the CANCELED section is still exactly Amelia Tyler and Persephone Valentine, unchanged."
